<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mauri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Maurusii</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mauri were the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> people of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, in what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, from whom the names Mauretania and Moors derive. United under kings by the late 3rd century BCE, they became Roman allies and then subjects after their kingdom was annexed in 42 CE. Mauri cavalry served widely in the Roman army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mauri.jpg" alt="Mauri" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lusius_Quietus_on_Column_of_Trajan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
